WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:03.136
-David Blaine,
great to see you, bud.

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:04.570
-Great to see you.

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:06.673
-I'm always happy to see you.

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:09.875
I'm always a little nervous
when I see you and anxious

00:00:09.875 --> 00:00:12.746
but always in a good way.
I mean, we've been through --

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:14.913
We've seen you --
I've sewed your lips shut

00:00:14.913 --> 00:00:17.850
with a needle and thread.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:21.120
-Well, let's try simple.
Let's try something simple.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.656
-Okay.
Okay.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:27.393
-Do you want to take out
the numbers or the pictures?

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:29.128
Number cards or picture cards?

00:00:29.128 --> 00:00:33.366
-Uh, uh, uh, uh...
Uh, pictures.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:34.467
-Okay.
-Yeah.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:36.535
-So, the pictures,
you have the Jacks,

00:00:36.535 --> 00:00:37.704
the Queens, or the Kings.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.806
Which ones do you want?
You decide.

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:42.242
-I like Jacks.
-Okay.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:45.111
The Jacks, you have a red Jack
or a black Jack.

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:46.880
Reds or blacks?
Which one do you want?

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:50.149
-I'm gonna say a black Jack.

00:00:50.149 --> 00:00:52.451
-By the way, you can change
your mind at any point.

00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:54.420
I don't want you to think
that I'm making you say this.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:55.889
Do you want to change?

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:58.224
-No, I'll stick with black Jack.
-Oh, you're good.

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:01.060
-So, the black Jacks,
you have clubs or spades.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:04.664
Which one do you want?
-I'll do clubs.

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:07.466
-By the way, nobody ever
changes, but you can.

00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:08.601
But it's up to you.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:11.371
-[ Laughing ]

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:13.606
-You're so in my head right now.
-I just want this to be fair.

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:15.608
So if you want to change
to the other one, you can.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.309
You can do whatever you want.
-Okay, great.

00:01:17.309 --> 00:01:19.579
Then I will change.

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:21.347
-To which one?
-I will say, uh --

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:24.650
-You want to go to
the spade or the club or...?

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:29.822
-I'll say -- I'll say --
I'll say the spade.

00:01:29.822 --> 00:01:32.191
-Are you sure?
Do you want to change back?

00:01:32.191 --> 00:01:34.861
-No, Jack of spades.

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:37.030
-You're sure?
-Yes.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.765
-Well, look, here,
I just want to show you

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:41.367
something funny in the deck.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:43.703
Here it is.
See, there's one card

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:46.205
that's a little different
than all the others.

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:49.475
And you can see, look,
the one card that' different

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:53.546
is in the middle, and it's --
see that one card?

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:57.116
It's a Jack of spades.
-[ Laughing ]

00:01:57.116 --> 00:02:00.053
But, Jimmy -- Jimmy --
No, but, Jimmy, listen to me.

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:03.590
It's possible
that I did some sleight of hand.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.991
When I was removing
the cards in the box,

00:02:05.991 --> 00:02:08.560
maybe I flicked it
really fast, correct?

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:12.332
-Sure.
-No, it's not possible.

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:15.334
'Cause this, the Jack of spades,

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:17.436
is the only red card
in this deck.

00:02:17.436 --> 00:02:19.471
See?

00:02:19.471 --> 00:02:21.841
Not only is it the only
red card in the deck,

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.342
but you're thinking, like,
"Oh, wait.

00:02:23.342 --> 00:02:25.344
Maybe he convinced me.
Maybe..."

00:02:25.344 --> 00:02:27.580
There's no other card
that would have worked.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.648
Only the Jack of spades
would have worked...

00:02:29.648 --> 00:02:31.184
-Yeah.
-...from the very beginning.

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:32.718
Look.

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:35.788
The whole deck...is blank.

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:38.858
-[ Laughing, clapping ]
-And that's...

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:42.895
I mean...
-Dude, you're unbelievable, man.

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:44.797
That is insanity.

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:46.565
-So, hold on.
I'm gonna --

00:02:46.565 --> 00:02:47.967
You can see all the cards.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.635
You can see all of the cards
in the deck.

00:02:49.635 --> 00:02:51.036
You can see
they're all different, yes?

00:02:51.036 --> 00:02:52.538
-Yes.
-So you thought of

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:55.708
a Jack of spades but you changed
from the Jack of clubs.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:58.377
But now I want you
to think of a new card

00:02:58.377 --> 00:03:01.548
that would be your favorite card
but one that I could never know.

00:03:01.548 --> 00:03:03.583
-Okay.

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:12.025
-[ Coughs ]

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:16.396
-[ Laughs ]
-[ Coughs ]

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:19.865
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:19.865 --> 00:03:21.700
-Wait. But, Jimmy...

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.603
What was the card
that you were thinking of?

00:03:24.603 --> 00:03:28.240
-It was different card.
It was 8 of hearts.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:31.177
-Oh, yeah, good.
That worked.

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:36.115
-[ Laughing ]

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:38.551
-[ Chuckles ]

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:42.922
-Oh, my...gosh!
Gosh!

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:45.758
-But you know the --
But, Jimmy, you know that

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:47.860
when you think of cards,
like, any card

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:51.096
that you would think of,
I would be able to produce.

00:03:51.096 --> 00:03:53.132
-Yeah.
-Doesn't make a difference.

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.667
-I don't know how --
-You know, like, any card

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:59.271
that you would choose --
-I don't -- I don't know how.

00:03:59.271 --> 00:04:00.306
I don't know how.

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:03.042
-Do you want me to tell you how?

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:05.044
-Sure.
-You want me to tell you how?

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:06.612
-No. Do I?

00:04:06.612 --> 00:04:10.149
-The reason I can
spit your card out of my mouth

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:13.252
is because
I have a secret assistant.

00:04:13.252 --> 00:04:15.554
You might remember him.

00:04:15.554 --> 00:04:19.025
He's grown a bit
since the last time you saw him.

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:20.559
-It's not a frog.
Please, no.

00:04:20.559 --> 00:04:22.294
Oh, my God.
Please don't do this.

00:04:22.294 --> 00:04:23.629
No, it's not.

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:26.332
You're not doing this.
[ Laughing ]

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:34.707
[ Laughing, rapping desk,
papers crumpling ]

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:40.279
[ Laughing ]

00:04:40.279 --> 00:04:43.916
What is going on?
What is going on?

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:45.651
You have to
stop doing that, man.

00:04:45.651 --> 00:04:49.054
That is un --
-This is my magical assistant.

00:04:49.054 --> 00:04:50.690
See.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:55.995
-He hands you different cards.
He's a very good -- oh, my gosh.

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:58.498
David, he's grow--
He's getting bi--

00:04:58.498 --> 00:04:59.966
Oh, my God.

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:04.503
David Blaine, we have
to talk about your new special,

00:05:04.503 --> 00:05:08.107
"The Ascension."
It's on YouTube August 31st.

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:10.976
From what I've heard about
"David Blaine: Ascension"

00:05:10.976 --> 00:05:13.479
is that --
[ Laughing ]

00:05:19.151 --> 00:05:21.754
-Sorry.
There was another one.

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:26.258
[ Both laugh ]

00:05:26.258 --> 00:05:29.795
-Oh!
Oh, my gosh.

00:05:29.795 --> 00:05:31.597
[ Breathes deeply ]

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:35.467
You have two assistants.
-Yeah.

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:37.670
No, but, so --
[ Laughs ]

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.539
So, the new one
that I'm working on,

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:43.409
it's called "Ascension,"
and the goal is I want to

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:45.310
take a bunch of balloons

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:48.881
and just float up into the sky
until I vanish.

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:51.183
My dream has always been --

00:05:51.183 --> 00:05:54.654
Looking up into the sky,
it would be amazing to just --

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:56.622
like the movie
"Le ballon rouge,"

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:59.224
just grab a bunch of balloons
and go drifting away.

00:05:59.224 --> 00:06:02.595
So I've been diligently
putting this together,

00:06:02.595 --> 00:06:05.131
and I have an amazing team.

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:08.033
And working with YouTube
has allowed me to kind of

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:12.605
just put together
this insane idea.

00:06:12.605 --> 00:06:14.606
-And hopefully
you're doing this safely.

00:06:14.606 --> 00:06:18.677
I mean, what --
-Yeah, we're doing it safely.

00:06:18.677 --> 00:06:20.512
And I've been practicing,

00:06:20.512 --> 00:06:25.417
and I had to get
a hot-air-balloon pilot license.

00:06:25.417 --> 00:06:28.153
I got my gas restriction lifted
so I could fly

00:06:28.153 --> 00:06:31.357
helium-filled balloons,
which is pretty rare, actually.

00:06:31.357 --> 00:06:35.260
And I've been
jumping out of airplanes

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:37.529
to get comfortable in the air.
-Really?

00:06:37.529 --> 00:06:41.333
Will you have a parachute
or anything?

00:06:41.333 --> 00:06:43.535
What if the balloons pop?

00:06:43.535 --> 00:06:46.839
-Yeah. Well, I would have one
up in the balloons.

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:52.177
'Cause I -- I want it to be
the image of just

00:06:52.177 --> 00:06:53.745
a boy holding
a bunch of balloons

00:06:53.745 --> 00:06:55.981
and drifting away
like the movie that I saw.

00:06:55.981 --> 00:06:57.749
So I want it to be simplistic.

00:06:57.749 --> 00:06:59.585
-I understand what
you want it to look like.

00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:03.722
You can always draw it.
You don't have to do it.

00:07:03.722 --> 00:07:07.426
-[ Laughs ]
So, behind me is some of the --

00:07:07.426 --> 00:07:09.561
We're in the warehouse,
actually.

00:07:09.561 --> 00:07:12.164
Behind me
is enough of the balloons

00:07:12.164 --> 00:07:14.500
that my daughter would --

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.802
This is enough to float
my daughter right here.

00:07:16.802 --> 00:07:20.572
So this is just
a little bit of the rig

00:07:20.572 --> 00:07:24.876
which we're gonna be using.
And then obviously, for me,

00:07:24.876 --> 00:07:27.780
it's much --
a much bigger rig.

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:33.952
And I'd say,
with 20 more of those balloons,

00:07:33.952 --> 00:07:36.321
I would go floating
all the way up

00:07:36.321 --> 00:07:39.425
and disappear into the sky
legitimately.

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:45.330
But, of course, anything over,
you know, 18,000 feet gets --

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:50.069
becomes more and more dangerous
because the temperatures drop,

00:07:50.069 --> 00:07:53.138
and you can become hypoxic
and things like that.

00:07:53.138 --> 00:07:56.108
So I've been practicing
and learning all of that.

00:07:56.108 --> 00:07:59.611
-This is August 31st this is
happening, live on YouTube.

00:07:59.611 --> 00:08:02.215
-Depending on the winds.
[ Laughs ]

00:08:02.215 --> 00:08:03.649
-Okay.
So, weather permitting, okay.

00:08:03.649 --> 00:08:04.750
'Cause you don't
want to end up --

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:06.818
-Weather permitting.
[ Both laugh ]

00:08:06.818 --> 00:08:08.621
-You're gonna end up
in California again,

00:08:08.621 --> 00:08:10.656
and you're gonna go, "Wait. What
happened to David Blaine?"

00:08:10.656 --> 00:08:12.624
"Oh, he's still floating.
Yeah."

00:08:12.624 --> 00:08:15.594
I cannot wait to see this.

00:08:15.594 --> 00:08:18.097
I'm psyched for you.

00:08:18.097 --> 00:08:20.499
Check out
"David Blaine: Ascension,"

00:08:20.499 --> 00:08:23.369
streaming live on YouTube
in just a few weeks,

00:08:23.369 --> 00:08:25.904
August 31st, weather permitting.

00:08:25.904 --> 00:08:27.672
David,
you're always a great guest.

00:08:27.672 --> 00:08:31.543
Please be safe, buddy.
I want to see you again, okay?

00:08:31.543 --> 00:08:33.212
-Thank you,
and thanks for having me again.

00:08:33.212 --> 00:08:34.380
Good to see you.

